  "source": "https://gc.nh.gov/rsa/html/LXIII/659/659-94.htm",
  "statuteText": "659:94 Write-In Vote. –\n\nIf a presidential candidate receives as write-in votes 10 percent or more, before any rounding to the nearest whole number, of the total votes cast for all such candidates of a political party, the secretary of state shall so notify in writing the person; and the person shall then select the number of delegates and alternates to which he is entitled according to RSA 659:93 and such delegates and alternates shall file the certification provided for in RSA 655:51."
}
